{"id":"assistant-identity","category":"assistant","question":"Who are you?","answer":"I’m Aether, New Era Designs’ document-guided studio assistant. I can explain Chris, the studio, services, process, project fit, technical terms, and next steps using the studio’s curated knowledge base. I do not invent answers or replace a project conversation with Chris.","keywords":"aether assistant chatbot bot ai artificial intelligence who are you help guide","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Talk with Chris"},
{"id":"studio-overview","category":"studio","question":"What is New Era Designs?","answer":"New Era Designs is Chris Edwards’ independent Houston-based design platform. The studio connects brand identity, digital communication, wayfinding, signage, environmental graphics, 3D spatial thinking, and production-aware documentation so an idea can survive the move from screen to physical space.","keywords":"new era designs studio company business agency platform overview about identity houston","url":"/pages/marketing-materials","linkLabel":"Explore the studio"},
{"id":"chris-overview","category":"studio","question":"Who is Chris Edwards?","answer":"Chris Edwards is a multidisciplinary designer focused on brand, spatial communication, signage, wayfinding, environmental graphics, digital experiences, and design documentation. His strength is seeing the complete system: what people notice, where they hesitate, how a space communicates, and what a fabricator or project team needs to execute the idea clearly.","keywords":"chris christopher edwards founder owner designer biography bio person background about","url":"/pages/cases","linkLabel":"View the work"},
{"id":"studio-purpose","category":"studio","question":"Why did Chris create New Era Designs?","answer":"New Era Designs gives Chris an independent platform for collaborating across businesses, architects, contractors, fabricators, and creative teams. It is a place to connect visual ambition with the technical and operational realities that turn a concept into a working brand, environment, or communication system.","keywords":"why founded origin story purpose mission platform independent created","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Start a conversation"},
{"id":"design-philosophy","category":"studio","question":"What is the New Era Designs philosophy?","answer":"Design should reduce friction, create memory, and make the next decision easier. New Era treats branding, digital touchpoints, signage, and space as one connected experience—not isolated decoration. The goal is clarity with personality and creativity that remains buildable.","keywords":"philosophy values belief approach design thinking clarity memory psychology transformation decoration","url":"/pages/info","linkLabel":"See the process"},
{"id":"studio-difference","category":"studio","question":"What makes New Era Designs different?","answer":"The studio works in the gap between 2D ideas and 3D reality. Chris combines visual direction with spatial psychology, fabrication awareness, technical documentation, stakeholder coordination, and a strong understanding of how people encounter brands in real environments.","keywords":"different unique advantage value proposition why choose new era multidisciplinary systems technical creative","url":"/pages/cases","linkLabel":"See the difference"},
{"id":"tone-personality","category":"studio","question":"What is the New Era Designs personality?","answer":"Direct, visually literate, curious, emotionally intelligent, technically grounded, and willing to tell the truth about scope, timing, and production. The work can be playful or luxurious, but the thinking stays precise and the client’s real constraints remain part of the design.","keywords":"voice tone personality style character communication direct luxury playful precise honest","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Meet the studio"},
{"id":"location","category":"studio","question":"Where is New Era Designs based?","answer":"New Era Designs is based in the Houston area and can collaborate remotely with clients and project partners in other cities. Site-dependent work may require photography, verified field information, local partners, or an on-site visit.","keywords":"where location located houston texas stafford remote nationwide national travel city","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Ask about your location"},
{"id":"services-overview","category":"services","question":"What services does New Era Designs offer?","answer":"Services can include discovery and strategy, brand identity systems, websites and digital experiences, wayfinding, signage, environmental graphics, message hierarchy, sign-family planning, 2D/3D visualization, design-intent documentation, presentation systems, marketing materials, vendor coordination, and ongoing design support.","keywords":"services capabilities offerings provide branding website digital ux ui wayfinding signage environmental graphics 3d documentation marketing","url":"/pages/marketing-materials","linkLabel":"Explore services"},
{"id":"brand-systems","category":"services","question":"Can you create a complete brand identity?","answer":"Yes. A brand engagement can connect positioning, visual identity, typography, color, graphic language, content hierarchy, templates, digital behavior, environmental applications, and practical rules that help the system remain consistent as the business grows.","keywords":"brand branding identity logo visual system typography color guidelines strategy positioning refresh rebrand","url":"/pages/marketing-materials","linkLabel":"Explore brand systems"},
{"id":"web-digital","category":"services","question":"Do you design websites and digital experiences?","answer":"Yes. Digital work can cover information architecture, UX/UI, responsive websites, Shopify theme design, content structure, interaction direction, prototypes, and reusable visual systems. The goal is a site that communicates clearly, works across screen sizes, and feels connected to the physical brand.","keywords":"website websites web digital ux ui ecommerce shopify responsive mobile desktop development interaction prototype","url":"/pages/marketing-materials","linkLabel":"Explore digital work"},
{"id":"signage","category":"services","question":"Do you design signage?","answer":"Yes. Signage work can include sign-family concepts, identification, directional, informational, regulatory, tenant, storefront, monument, pylon, channel-letter, dimensional-letter, directory, and environmental applications—scoped according to the property and project team.","keywords":"sign signs signage channel letters monument pylon directory storefront tenant directional identification regulatory","url":"/pages/marketing-materials","linkLabel":"Explore signage"},
{"id":"wayfinding","category":"services","question":"What is wayfinding, and do you provide it?","answer":"Wayfinding is the complete system that helps people orient themselves and move through an environment. New Era can map visitor flow and decision points, structure destination names and message hierarchy, plan sign types and locations, and develop the visual language that guides people without overwhelming them.","keywords":"wayfinding navigation directions orient visitor flow decision points maps destination directional signs","url":"/pages/marketing-materials","linkLabel":"Explore wayfinding"},
{"id":"environmental-graphics","category":"services","question":"What are environmental graphics?","answer":"Environmental graphics bring identity and information into physical space through murals, supergraphics, window and wall applications, dimensional elements, donor or history displays, branded moments, and other architectural-scale communication. They can support navigation, storytelling, placemaking, and atmosphere.","keywords":"environmental graphics egd experiential murals wall graphics supergraphics placemaking branded environment spatial","url":"/pages/marketing-materials","linkLabel":"Explore spatial design"},
{"id":"visualization","category":"services","question":"Do you provide 3D visualization or mockups?","answer":"Yes. Depending on scope, New Era can use scaled elevations, contextual mockups, SketchUp-based spatial models, placement studies, and presentation views to test scale, visibility, material direction, and how an idea relates to its environment before production.","keywords":"3d three dimensional visualization render rendering mockup sketchup model elevation placement scale context","url":"/pages/cases","linkLabel":"View visual studies"},
{"id":"marketing-materials","category":"services","question":"Can you design marketing materials?","answer":"Yes. New Era can extend a brand into presentations, proposals, brochures, social content systems, campaign graphics, print collateral, event material, and reusable templates. The deliverables are defined around how the team actually needs to communicate and produce content.","keywords":"marketing materials collateral brochure flyer presentation proposal social media campaign print templates content","url":"/pages/marketing-materials","linkLabel":"Explore marketing work"},
{"id":"industries","category":"fit","question":"What industries does New Era Designs serve?","answer":"The studio is especially aligned with commercial real estate, retail, restaurants, hospitality, fitness and amenities, offices, mixed-use properties, cultural or educational environments, design and fabrication partners, and growing businesses that need a connected brand, digital, or spatial system.","keywords":"industries sectors commercial real estate retail restaurant hospitality hotel fitness office mixed use cultural education clients","url":"/pages/cases","linkLabel":"View relevant work"},
{"id":"client-fit","category":"fit","question":"Who is the ideal client?","answer":"A strong fit is a client who values clarity, shares the necessary information, names a decision-maker, respects production realities, and wants a design system rather than disconnected files. New Era can plug into an existing team or help structure a project that is still taking shape.","keywords":"ideal client fit right for me business organization decision maker collaboration project fit","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Check project fit"},
{"id":"small-business","category":"fit","question":"Do you work with small businesses?","answer":"Yes, when the goals and scope are a good match. A smaller business may start with a focused identity, website, storefront, signage, or communication problem and build the broader system in phases rather than trying to purchase everything at once.","keywords":"small business startup entrepreneur local company budget phased affordable","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Describe your project"},
{"id":"architect-fabricator-fit","category":"fit","question":"Can New Era support architects, contractors, or fabricators?","answer":"Yes. New Era can support a larger project team with visual concepts, elevations, message and location planning, presentation material, design-intent packages, brand interpretation, client-facing visuals, and review coordination. Exact responsibilities are defined in writing so design, engineering, fabrication, and installation roles stay clear.","keywords":"architect architects contractor contractors fabricator fabricators sign shop vendor installer partner support outsource white label","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Discuss team support"},
{"id":"process-overview","category":"process","question":"What is your project process?","answer":"A typical engagement moves through discovery and scoping, site or asset review, strategy, concept design, message hierarchy or system planning, visualization, documentation, review, and handoff. Larger spatial projects may add bid support, shop-drawing review, production coordination, installation QA, and closeout. Only the phases named in the approved scope are included.","keywords":"process workflow phases steps discovery concept design documentation review handoff production closeout","url":"/pages/info","linkLabel":"See the process"},
{"id":"start-project","category":"process","question":"How do I start a project?","answer":"Send a concise description of what you are building, what is not working, who needs to use it, the location or platform, desired timing, known budget, and any existing plans or brand assets. New Era can then recommend the right discovery step and scope.","keywords":"start begin contact hire book inquiry consultation proposal kickoff project","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Start a project"},
{"id":"inputs-needed","category":"process","question":"What information should I prepare?","answer":"Useful inputs include goals, audience, site address or platform, current pain points, existing brand files, plans or measurements, photographs, destination or tenant lists, technical constraints, decision-makers, budget range, schedule, vendor contacts, and examples of what success should feel or function like.","keywords":"prepare need provide files assets plans photos measurements brief questionnaire information inputs","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Send project details"},
{"id":"deliverables","category":"process","question":"What deliverables might I receive?","answer":"Deliverables depend on scope and may include strategy summaries, mood or concept directions, identity assets, responsive page designs, prototypes, sign-family drawings, elevations, location plans, message schedules, visualizations, standards documents, presentation PDFs, production-ready artwork, and organized handoff files.","keywords":"deliverables receive files outputs package drawings artwork standards pdf source files handoff","url":"/pages/marketing-materials","linkLabel":"Review capabilities"},
{"id":"timeline","category":"process","question":"How long does a project take?","answer":"Timing depends on scope, site complexity, number of stakeholders, speed of approvals, and whether engineering, permitting, fabrication, or installation partners are involved. A focused design task may take weeks; a multi-phase wayfinding or environmental system can take several months. The proposal defines the working schedule.","keywords":"timeline time duration how long weeks months schedule deadline rush","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Discuss timing"},
{"id":"pricing","category":"process","question":"How much does a project cost?","answer":"Pricing is scoped around complexity, phases, deliverables, schedule, number of locations or sign types, stakeholder load, and the level of technical or production coordination required. Share your goals, timing, and working budget so New Era can recommend a focused scope instead of guessing.","keywords":"price pricing cost costs budget fee fees quote estimate investment rate rates affordable","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Request a proposal"},
{"id":"revisions","category":"process","question":"How do revisions and approvals work?","answer":"Review rounds and approval milestones are defined in the proposal. Clear consolidated feedback from the authorized decision-maker keeps the project moving. Changes to approved work, project sequence, or scope may require a written change order before additional work begins.","keywords":"revision revisions changes feedback approvals rounds change order scope creep","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Ask about the workflow"},
{"id":"retainers","category":"process","question":"Do you offer retainers or ongoing support?","answer":"Yes. Ongoing support can be structured for recurring brand, property, signage, content, digital, documentation, or design-governance needs. The right arrangement depends on request volume, response expectations, and whether the work is predictable or project-based.","keywords":"retainer monthly ongoing support subscription maintenance design partner hours","url":"/pages/retainer-services","linkLabel":"Explore retainers"},
{"id":"remote-collaboration","category":"process","question":"Can the project be completed remotely?","answer":"Many brand, digital, visualization, and documentation tasks can be completed remotely. Spatial projects still need reliable site information; that may come from an on-site visit, verified drawings and measurements, a local partner, or a structured photo and video survey.","keywords":"remote virtual distance online site visit travel measurements collaboration","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Discuss logistics"},
{"id":"fabrication-boundary","category":"technical","question":"Does New Era fabricate or install signs?","answer":"New Era primarily provides strategy, design, visualization, coordination, and design-intent documentation. Physical fabrication and installation are excluded unless explicitly added to a written scope through qualified partners. The fabricator remains responsible for manufacturing means, methods, and shop drawings.","keywords":"fabricate fabrication manufacture manufacturing install installation signs sign shop build physical production excluded","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Discuss production"},
{"id":"engineering-boundary","category":"technical","question":"Does New Era provide engineering or stamped drawings?","answer":"No—not as a default design service. New Era’s drawings communicate design intent. Structural engineering, electrical engineering, stamped construction documents, and other licensed professional services must be provided by the appropriate engineer, architect, fabricator, or contractor unless separately coordinated in writing.","keywords":"engineering engineer stamped drawings structural electrical architectural construction documents licensed","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Clarify project roles"},
{"id":"permitting-boundary","category":"technical","question":"Does New Era handle permits?","answer":"Permitting, permit filing, expediting, and final code determination are not automatically included. New Era can prepare or coordinate design information that supports a permit package when scoped, while the responsible licensed vendor or project professional verifies local requirements and submits the final application.","keywords":"permit permits permitting city code municipal filing expediting approval compliance","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Discuss permit support"},
{"id":"ada-boundary","category":"technical","question":"Can New Era help with ADA and accessibility?","answer":"Accessibility is considered during planning and design, including hierarchy, legibility, mounting logic, and tactile or room-identification needs when relevant. New Era does not provide legal certification. Final ADA, TAS, building-code, and jurisdictional compliance must be verified by the responsible qualified professional.","keywords":"ada tas accessibility accessible braille tactile compliance legal certification code","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Discuss accessibility"},
{"id":"design-intent","category":"technical","question":"What are design-intent drawings?","answer":"Design-intent drawings communicate what a design should look like and how it should relate to the site: dimensions, materials, colors, typography, placement, hierarchy, and visual details. They guide the fabricator but are not a substitute for engineered shop drawings or field verification.","keywords":"design intent drawings elevations dimensions materials colors placement specifications documentation","url":"/pages/marketing-materials","linkLabel":"Explore documentation"},
{"id":"shop-drawings","category":"technical","question":"What is the difference between design intent and shop drawings?","answer":"Design intent defines the approved visual and functional direction. Shop drawings are produced by the fabricator to explain exactly how an item will be manufactured, wired, supported, mounted, and installed. New Era may review shop drawings for visual conformance when that review is included in scope.","keywords":"shop drawings fabrication drawings difference design intent manufacturer wiring mounting hardware review","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Plan the handoff"},
{"id":"message-hierarchy","category":"technical","question":"What is message hierarchy?","answer":"Message hierarchy determines which information people need first, second, and later. In wayfinding, that may mean property, zone, building, level, destination, and room. A disciplined hierarchy prevents signs from becoming crowded and helps visitors make one clear decision at a time.","keywords":"message hierarchy information naming nomenclature destinations sign copy content order","url":"/pages/marketing-materials","linkLabel":"Explore wayfinding strategy"},
{"id":"decision-points","category":"technical","question":"What is a decision point?","answer":"A decision point is a place where someone must choose between paths—such as an entrance, intersection, elevator lobby, corridor split, or parking exit. Wayfinding information belongs before or at that moment, where it can prevent hesitation and wrong turns.","keywords":"decision point intersection entrance corridor elevator parking choose route navigation wayfinding","url":"/pages/marketing-materials","linkLabel":"Explore wayfinding"},
{"id":"progressive-disclosure","category":"technical","question":"What is progressive disclosure in wayfinding?","answer":"Progressive disclosure means showing only the information needed for the next decision, then revealing more detail as the visitor gets closer. It reduces cognitive overload and keeps large destination lists from competing with the most important direction.","keywords":"progressive disclosure wayfinding cognitive overload information signs navigation destinations","url":"/pages/marketing-materials","linkLabel":"Explore wayfinding"},
{"id":"portfolio","category":"work","question":"Where can I see the portfolio or case studies?","answer":"The Cases page brings together selected work and concept studies. Project labels distinguish client work, professional contributions, independent concepts, and speculative studies so the context of each piece remains clear.","keywords":"portfolio work projects cases case studies examples clients gallery selected work concept studies","url":"/pages/cases","linkLabel":"View selected work"},
{"id":"protected-work","category":"work","question":"Can I view private or protected projects?","answer":"Some work may be protected because of client, employer, partnership, or project-access requirements. Use the protected-project route or contact the studio with the type of work you need to evaluate. Access is handled case by case.","keywords":"private protected password confidential nda work portfolio access projects","url":"/pages/protected-projects-1","linkLabel":"Request project access"},
{"id":"podcast","category":"content","question":"What is the New Era podcast about?","answer":"The podcast is the studio’s more open cultural channel: conversations about fashion, luxury, design, identity, power, taste, creative work, and the systems behind what people value. It shares New Era’s visual energy without being limited to commercial signage or client services.","keywords":"podcast show episodes audio fashion luxury culture design identity opinions listen cd","url":"/pages/podcast","linkLabel":"Visit the podcast"},
{"id":"hire-chris","category":"career","question":"Can I hire Chris for a role or creative collaboration?","answer":"Yes. Chris is open to conversations about senior design, brand experience, environmental graphics, spatial design, art direction, digital design, and project-based creative collaboration. Share the role, team, location, responsibilities, timing, and portfolio needs through the contact page.","keywords":"hire chris job employment freelance contract role career resume collaborate art director senior designer","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Contact Chris"},
{"id":"education-experience","category":"career","question":"What is Chris’s professional background?","answer":"Chris studied visual and digital design, developed experience across print production, marketing, retail presentation, branding, and client-facing creative work, and expanded into signage, spatial systems, 3D visualization, and fabrication-aware documentation. That range supports his cross-disciplinary approach today.","keywords":"education school background experience resume career history adobe print production marketing retail training","url":"/pages/cases","linkLabel":"See the work"},
{"id":"privacy","category":"assistant","question":"Does this chatbot collect or send my messages anywhere?","answer":"This version works inside your browser against a curated knowledge list. It does not send your question to an external AI model or store it on a New Era server. Avoid entering confidential project details; use the contact page when you are ready to discuss protected information directly.","keywords":"privacy data collect store save messages external ai model api confidential secure","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Contact securely"},
{"id":"confidence","category":"assistant","question":"What happens if Aether does not know the answer?","answer":"Aether will say when the knowledge base does not support a confident answer and route you to Chris. That is intentional: project-specific pricing, legal or code decisions, private work, availability, and unusual technical conditions need human review rather than a made-up response.","keywords":"dont know cannot answer fallback confidence wrong hallucination human chris specific question","url":"/pages/contact","linkLabel":"Ask Chris"}
